    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0685" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.51/58</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi>
                </p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Ambassador presents his compliments to the Secretary of State, and
                    has the honour to refer to the Department’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of November 29th last<anchor n="46" xml:id="d732-f1"/>
                    suggesting that immediate consideration be given to ways and means whereby the
                    British and United States Governments might assist the Government of Saudi
                    Arabia in fiscal and currency problems, and that informal discussion to this end
                    be held in Washington.</p>
                <pb facs="0686" n="674" xml:id="pg674"/>
                <p>2. His Majesty’s Government in the United Kingdom agree to this proposal, and
                    instructions have been issued to the United Kingdom Treasury Delegation in
                    Washington to get in touch with representatives of the United States Treasury to
                    this end.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d732-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-01">February 1,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d732-f1" n="46" xml:id="d732-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1943v04#pg_914">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, p. 914</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d732-f2" n="47" xml:id="d732-f2-content">
                <p>Meetings of officers from the Department, the Treasury Department, and the
                    British Embassy began on February 17, 1944, and continued through much of the
                    year.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
